All working. Here's a summary of the two APIs demonstrated:

| API | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `options.GetTypeInfo<T>()` | Returns `JsonTypeInfo<T>` directly — throws if unavailable |
| `options.TryGetTypeInfo<T>(out JsonTypeInfo<T>?)` | Returns `bool`; sets the out param if found, **never throws** |

The key code:

```csharp
// Strongly-typed metadata retrieval
JsonTypeInfo<Person> personInfo = options.GetTypeInfo<Person>();

// Safe probe — no exception if the type isn't known
if (options.TryGetTypeInfo<int[]>(out JsonTypeInfo<int[]>? info))
    // use info
else
    // not available
```

The "restricted options" part uses a source-generated context that only knows about `Person`, so `TryGetTypeInfo<int[]>` returns `false` without throwing.
